      "level": 2,
      "content": "FORCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Newton's First Law provides the qualitative definition of force and establishes the concept of inertia.",
        "Newton's Second Law provides the quantitative definition of force (F = ma) and relates force to rate of change of momentum.",
        "Newton's Third Law states that to every action there is an equal and opposite reaction acting on two different objects.",
        "Linear momentum (p = mv) is conserved in an isolated system where no external force acts.",
        "Friction is a contact force that opposes relative motion between two surfaces in contact."
      ],
      "id": "hbdcngu"
    },
