      "content": "TYPES OF FORCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "w23lnt9",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Contact Force – Requires physical contact Example: Friction, Muscular force",
        "Non-Contact Force – Acts from a distance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "olhxv51",
      "content": "Example: Gravitational force, Magnetic force, Electrostatic force"
    },
    {
      "id": "n3niu0h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NEWTON’S FIRST LAW OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "czhoj69",
      "content": "Statement:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "39owcra",
      "content": "An object remains at rest or in uniform motion in a straight line unless acted upon by an external force."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iwagcyj",
      "content": "This law is also known as the Law of Inertia. Inertia:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2ws82j7",
      "content": "The tendency of an object to resist change in its state of motion."
    },
    {
      "id": "en88v0t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Types of Inertia"
    },
    {
      "id": "iv54x1q",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Inertia of Rest",
        "Inertia of Motion",
        "Inertia of Direction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t61g3l6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NEWTON’S SECOND LAW OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s16yoea",
      "content": "Statement:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dmcvg9a",
      "content": "The rate of change of momentum of an object is directly proportional to the applied force and takes place in the direction of force."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "85gdob6",
      "content": "Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "To every action, there is always an equal and opposite reaction.",
      "id": "agzz8c3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1z2zklg",
      "content": "Force = Mass × Acceleration F = ma"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s61jgdk",
      "content": "SI Unit of Force = Newton"
    },
    {
      "id": "u1me1wr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MOMENTUM"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w46rmlk",
      "content": "Momentum is the product of mass and velocity. Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v7706u3",
      "content": "Momentum = Mass × Velocity p = mv"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gm0s7h1",
      "content": "Unit: kg m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "g3n6uoj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NEWTON’S THIRD LAW OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zk7u4hu",
      "content": "Statement:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2dmtp3x",
      "content": "For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Property",
        "Static Friction",
        "Kinetic Friction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "State of Motion",
          "Operates when the body is at rest relative to the surface",
          "Operates when the body is in relative motion"
        ],
        [
          "Magnitude",
          "Self-adjusting from zero up to a maximum limit",
          "Constant in magnitude once motion begins"
        ],
        [
          "Relative Value",
          "Higher maximum threshold (Limiting Friction)",
          "Slightly lower than maximum static friction"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "887nzpt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4mn6jqi",
      "content": "Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "81fvow5",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Walking</li><li>Swimming</li><li>Recoil of gun</li></ul>",
        "Walking",
        "Swimming",
        "Recoil of gun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "forxn3c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "LAW OF CONSERVATION OF MOMENTUM"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "06rpyq7",
      "content": "According to this law, the total momentum of a system remains constant if no external force acts on it."
    },
    {
      "id": "r3pvklh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FRICTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z3knn8y",
      "content": "Friction is the force that opposes motion between two surfaces in contact. Types of Friction:"
    },
    {
      "id": "183bhmg",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Static friction",
        "Sliding friction",
        "Rolling friction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "duzrpi9",
      "content": "Rolling friction is the least."
    },
    {
      "id": "a7dffcz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ADVANTAGES AND DISADVANTAGES OF FRICTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9212nem",
      "content": "Advantages:"
    },
    {
      "id": "5eft1xe",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Helps in walking</li><li>Writing is possible</li><li>Vehicles move due to friction</li></ul>",
        "Helps in walking",
        "Writing is possible",
        "Vehicles move due to friction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9joge8i",
      "content": "Disadvantages:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Inertia depends strictly on the mass of an object; higher mass means higher inertia.",
        "Recoil velocity of a gun and rocket propulsion are direct applications of the Law of Conservation of Momentum.",
        "Limiting friction is the maximum value of static friction and is always slightly greater than kinetic friction.",
        "Impulse is defined as Force × Time and is equal to the total change in momentum."
      ],
      "id": "vroe9c9"
    },
    {
      "id": "i9cjfy9",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Causes wear and tear</li><li>Produces heat</li><li>Reduces efficiency</li></ul>",
        "Causes wear and tear",
        "Produces heat",
        "Reduces efficiency"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "qj1lpq5",
